Matrix SSH is dependent on three primary libraries
*libssh-devel
*libhttp-cpp
*sqlute3-devel
*gcc
*g++

Witch need to be instealled onto a Linux system. These depend on the disto
so you will need to consult your package managers sources to aquire the pacakages
needed.

The process to compile is simple as all things relating to compiling MatrixSSH
is stored in MatrixSSHCompilerScrip.sh and should run on a Linux system.

The inital pacakge was built and test compiled on Fedora 44 (Fedora 44 KDE edition
to be percise) and tested on Rock Linux 10 (Dekstop is the KDE version but that
should not have an effect on running matirx SSH on Rocky Linux)